-- title:
--   Zariski sheaf property of the relative Pic⁰ presheaf under finite-map data
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a reduced Noetherian commutative ring, let $C$ be a scheme and $c\colon C\to\operatorname{Spec}R$ a proper morphism which is smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$, i.e. a morphism $\operatorname{Spec}R\to C$ whose composite with $c$ is the identity. Assume that $(c,\varepsilon)$ admits finite-map data of arbitrarily large degree: for every $m_0\in\mathbb N$ there is a `SmoothProperCurve.FiniteMapData` $\mathfrak F$ for $c$ and $\varepsilon$ with $m_0\le\mathfrak F.m$, that is, affine opens $U,V\subseteq C$ with $U\sqcup V=\top$, sections $f\in\Gamma(C,U)$, $g\in\Gamma(C,V)$ and an integer $m$ such that $U$ is exactly the complement of the image of $\varepsilon$, $U\sqcap V$ equals both $C_f$ and $C_g$, the restrictions of $f$ and $g$ to $U\sqcap V$ are mutually inverse, the $R$-algebra maps $R[X]\to\Gamma(C,U)$, $X\mapsto f$ and $R[X]\to\Gamma(C,V)$, $X\mapsto g$ (for the algebra structures induced by $c$) are finite, and for every local $R$-algebra $S$ and every $s\in S$ the quotient $S\otimes_R\Gamma(C,U)$ by the ideal generated by $1\otimes f-s\otimes 1$ is a finite free $S$-module of rank $m$. Then the presheaf `relSubPicPresheaf c ε (algEquivZeroCut c ε)` on $(\mathrm{Over}(\operatorname{Spec}R))^{\mathrm{op}}$ — the subfunctor of the relative Picard presheaf of $(c,\varepsilon)$ picking out, over an $R$-scheme $t\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}R$, those classes of rigidified line bundles $M$ satisfying `FibrewiseAlgEquivZero`, namely that for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every $s\colon\operatorname{Spec}k\to T$ the pullback of $M.L$ to the fibre `fibreAt c t s` is algebraically equivalent to zero — satisfies the sheaf condition `Presieve.IsSheaf` for the Zariski topology induced on the over-category of $\operatorname{Spec}R$.
--
--   This is the descent (sheaf) property of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ functor of a pointed smooth proper curve with geometrically integral fibres, in the edition whose hypotheses are a reduced Noetherian base together with finite-map data of unbounded degree. It is the input to the constructions of open charts for, and of a representing scheme for, the fibrewise-algebraically-trivial part of the relative Picard functor.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_RelPicard_isSheaf_relSubPicPresheaf_algEquivZeroCut_zariski_of_finiteMapData.lean

